  "final_message": "Customers with no payment method now enter dunning. The 24 existing tests pass, but I didn't add a test for the no-payment-method case, so the new path isn't covered.\n\n**Root cause:** `collect` in `billing/payments.py` returned `None` as soon as the customer had no default payment method. It never called `record_failure`, which is what increments `attempt_count`, emits `invoice.payment_failed`, schedules `next_attempt_at` and moves the subscription to `past_due`. So the invoice stayed open with nothing scheduled.\n\n**Fix:** that branch now calls `record_failure(ctx, invoice, \"no_payment_method\")` before returning `None`. This matches how the expired-card branch already behaves.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` as `{\"file\": \"payments.py\", \"function\": \"collect\"}`.",
